  "notes": "USAGE: Functions as a noun and as a する verb (あんよする = to walk, for babies).\n\nMILESTONE: あんよ is often used to describe a baby's developmental milestone of learning to walk.\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- あんよが{上手|じょうず} (good at walking - praise for toddlers)\n- よちよちあんよ (toddling walk)\n\nRELATED BABY TALK WORDS:\n- おてて (hands)\n- おめめ (eyes)\n- ねんね (sleep)\n- まんま (food)",
